Refuse a guest that connects from the host's own computer.

A client on the same computer that connects to its own host streams the
desktop back into itself, input included. The established path is the
address that answered the connectivity check with the attempt's
credentials, so when it is one of this computer's interface addresses (or
loopback) the attempt is ended and logged. Candidate addresses alone are
not trusted, because container bridges and virtual networks repeat across
computers. A peer that is not recognised is admitted as before.

